## Important improvement
There is one logic issue in `updateStatus()`:
```ts
if (latency > settings.threshold || errorRate > 3) {
  // degraded
} else if (latency > settings.threshold * 1.5 || errorRate > 4.5) {
  // critical
}
```

This should be reversed so `critical` is checked first. Correct version:

```ts
function updateStatus(latency: number, errorRate: number): void {
  systemStatusEl.className = "value status";

  if (latency > settings.threshold * 1.5 || errorRate > 4.5) {
    systemStatusEl.textContent = "Critical";
    systemStatusEl.classList.add("bad");
  } else if (latency > settings.threshold || errorRate > 3) {
    systemStatusEl.textContent = "Degraded";
    systemStatusEl.classList.add("warn");
  } else {
    systemStatusEl.textContent = "Healthy";
    systemStatusEl.classList.add("ok");
  }
}
```

