# Why this is a good initial implementation

## 1. Sharded routing
Messages are routed to worker queues by hash:
```rust
fn route(route_key: u64) -> usize {
    (route_key as usize) % NUM_WORKERS
}
```

This spreads load and preserves per-key ordering within a shard.

## 2. Bounded queues
```rust
bounded::<Message>(QUEUE_CAPACITY)
```
This prevents unbounded memory growth and gives explicit drop/backpressure behavior.

## 3. Latency monitoring
Each message carries `created_at`, and workers measure end-to-end queue+processing latency:
```rust
let latency = now.duration_since(msg.created_at).as_micros() as u64;
```

## 4. Histogram-based percentiles
Using `hdrhistogram` allows tracking p50/p95/p99 efficiently.

## 5. Cheap atomics for counters
Counters use `AtomicU64`, which is appropriate for high-rate metric collection.

