Raw sockets incur kernel overhead. Production-grade low-latency packet forwarding generally uses:
- DPDK
- XDP/eBPF
- AF_XDP
- netmap
- hardware RSS, hugepages, CPU pinning, busy polling
- zero-copy ring buffers
- NIC queue affinity and batching

