## Example: parsing delimited fields without allocation

Here’s a helper to split a line by a delimiter without creating new strings:

```rust
pub fn for_each_field<F>(record: &[u8], delim: u8, mut f: F)
where
    F: FnMut(&[u8]),
{
    let mut start = 0;
    for i in 0..record.len() {
        if record[i] == delim {
            f(&record[start..i]);
            start = i + 1;
        }
    }
    f(&record[start..]);
}
```

