## Current limitations

This is intentionally minimal. It does **not yet** include:

- Rigid body to rigid body collision detection
- Contact manifolds
- Constraint solver
- Broadphase / narrowphase collision acceleration
- Full inertia tensor rotation into world space
- Sleeping/deactivation
- Continuous collision detection
- Joints
- Multithreading
- SIMD optimization

Also, angular dynamics here are simplified. For general rigid bodies, you'd normally transform inertia tensors into world space each frame and use a more complete rotational integration scheme.

