# 8. Important gaps before production

A large financial institution would require all of the following before real use:

## Security
- OAuth2/JWT or mTLS client authentication
- fine-grained authorization
- encryption at rest and in transit
- secrets in Vault/HSM-backed systems
- request signing where appropriate
- PCI DSS controls if card data exists
- payload minimization and tokenization

## Reliability
- proper asynchronous processing
- transactional outbox pattern
- retries with backoff
- circuit breakers
- dead-letter queues
- idempotency race handling with locking or unique insert strategy

## Financial correctness
- double-entry ledger integration
- reservation/hold model
- reconciliation jobs
- immutable journal
- decimal precision rules per currency
- cutoff and settlement window logic
- duplicate detection beyond idempotency key

## Compliance
- sanctions screening
- AML monitoring
- audit immutability
- retention policies
- GDPR/PII handling
- maker-checker workflow
- legal entity and jurisdictional controls

## Operability
- correlation IDs
- structured logging
- distributed tracing
- SLOs/SLIs
- dashboards and alerting
- blue/green or canary deployments

